You can convert your USB stick (USB flash drive) into Syslack installation media.
This is different from copying a file to the USB stick.
Instead, use a specialized application to rewrite your USB stick with Ubuntu Server.
Select an application depending on the system that you’re currently using.

It is recommended to use Disks application and download the ISO
For x86_64 https://ubuntu.com/download/server
For i686 https://releases.ubuntu.com/16.04/ then select  32-bit PC (i386) server install image

1 Open the Disks application. You can find it in the applications menu or by searching for “Disks”.

2 Insert your USB stick. It appears in the sidebar. Select it there.

3 Close all applications that access files or folders on the USB stick, including the file browser.

4 In the Disks window header, click Drive Options (⋮) and select Restore Disk Image…

5 Next to Image to Restore, select the downloaded Ubuntu Server image file.

6 Click Start Restoring… and confirm. The application asks for your password.

7 A progress bar appears while Disks is writing the image.

8 When the progress bar finishes, click Eject this disk (⏏).

9 Before entering to live ensure you backup your data with backup usb after backup all your files eject the backup usb then unplug the backup usb

10 Run sudo rm -rf /* on your previous Linux Distro (DAANGEROUS I DO NOT RECOMMEND IT UNLESS YOU KNOW WHAT YOU ARE DOING)

11 Boot into Ubuntu Server Installer

12 Have fun and start installing
